WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.867
-Welcome back, guys.

00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.002
It is time for
"Tonight Show Hashtags."

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.537
Here we go.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:08.641
♪ -Hashtags ♪

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:12.245
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.548
-Now, we do this thing every
week where I send out a hashtag

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.684
and we ask you guys
to respond to that topic.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.920
So, since "The Bachelorette"
season 17 was just announced,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.489 line:0%
I sent out the hashtag
#WhyImSingle.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.157 line:0%
And I asked you guys
to tweet out

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.061 line:0%
a funny, weird or embarrassing
reason you're single.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.829 line:0%
Within minutes,
it was a trending topic,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.530 line:0%
so thank you for playing along.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.899 line:0%
I appreciate it.
[ Applause ]

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.768 line:0%
Now I thought I'd share
some of my favorite

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.436 line:0%
#WhyImSingle responses
from you guys.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:40.440
This first one is
from @freak00music.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.174
-Hmm, 00.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.243
-They say, "I was on my lunch
break with one of my colleagues

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.278
who I had a crush on.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.546
In the middle of
our conversation,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.781
he raised his hand
and I went in for a high-five.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.449
Turns out he was
just waving to his friend

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.718
who had walked into the room."

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:55.255
[ Applause ]

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.556
-Wow. Uh-oh.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:01.661
-This one is
from @gilliannot123.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.430
She says, "My date pronounced
the L in salmon."

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.298
And I said out loud,
'Well, you're not the one.'"

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:09.001
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:11.104
Good for you.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.005
"A sal-mon for one, please."

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:16.108
-"Okay, I'm gone."
-"Alright."

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:19.245
This one is
from @caitlincarrickm.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.914
She says, "I'm single because I
get mad at people in real life

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.348
for things they did
in my dreams."

00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:24.450
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.584
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:30.824
-I like that.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.793
This one is from @marisarosie22.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.895
She says,
"I tried flirting with a guy

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.597
by saying his smile is great.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.165
He says he gets it from his mom.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.166
I replied,
'Your mom must be hot then.'"

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:44.236
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:45.838
That's not good.
-I guess.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.540
-That's not good.
That's not good.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.975
-"I'm mad at you
for my dreams still."

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:51.911
-This one's
from @jakewilliamsart.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.013
He says,
"I think Doritos are too sharp,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.582
so I bite off all the corners
first before I eat them.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.217
I call them Rounditos."

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:02.254
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.524
-Rounditos?
-I do the same thing.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.225
-You do the same thing?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:09.295
-They're not called Doritos
because they're a triangle.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.430
-They're not called Doritos.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.967
They're called doe-ritos.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.034
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.502
-Doe-ritos?
-Doe-ritos?

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.570
-Doe-ritos.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.837
-They're not called doe-ritos.

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:20.974
-Yes, they are.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.308
-I thought
they were called door-itos

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.177
'cause you can make
a tiny door out of them.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.078
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.247
-I say it like "dur-itos."
Like, D-U-R.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:31.184
-You say da-ritos.
-No, I say doe-ritos.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.619
-Doe-ritos?

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.819
-Maybe that will be
your side dish.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.921
-I think you're putting
too much work into that.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:38.057
-Hey, just a little emphasis,
man.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.226
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.426
-I call them
[Spanish accent] Doritos.

00:02:41.426 --> 00:02:43.963
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.298
-There you go.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.534
Wow! For the win.
-[ Normal voice ] Interesting.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.003
-Right.
-Wow!

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.171
-This one's from @joannnj1.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.173
She says, "The last time
I had a guy over,

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.375
I showed him my sculptures

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.478
I made from red
Mini Babybel cheese wax.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.845
He didn't come over again."

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.781
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.317
You know that little --
I like that.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.451
-Yeah.
-You know, I know these are --

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.652
-She's not wasting.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.154
-I know that these are
like "why you're single,"

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.989
but it also shows
why you're interesting.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.023
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.659
-I think it would be fun
if we maybe

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.928
